WEBVTT

00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:07.050
The Friendship Cup, where losers are sent to 
do hard labor underground for life, is wrong.

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.570
That's what I told people, but...

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.590
Somewhere inside me,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:17.780
I realized I had a desire to be stronger 
than anyone and pursue victory.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.600
And a feeling of powerlessness, too.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.070
I can't save Sawatari from 
being sent underground.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.280
I can't save Gongenzaka or Mr. 
Tokumatsu or Tsukikage...

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.680
S-Sawatari...

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:40.540
D-Wheels.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.800
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.480
which are an evolution of duel disks.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:49.900
They combine speed and thrills to make the ultimate show,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.060
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:30.230
The Losers Who Crawl in the Dirt

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.930
Let me go already!

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:36.190
Where are you people taking me?

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:40.010
Didn't you hear what Yuya Sakaki said earlier?

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.000
Losers in the Friendship Cup 
are sent underground.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.480
And they can never return to the surface.

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:49.820
Who made these rules?

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.270
I don't acknowledge them! 
They don't apply to me!

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:54.410
Whether you acknowledge them or not,

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:58.090
the place you're going now is known as "hell."

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.070
Hell?

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.230
It has its own rules.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:04.350
On our way there, we'll teach them to you.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.210
If you want to survive, you'll listen closely.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.440
Yes... This place is hell on Earth.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.100
Those who lose on the surface world, 
those who are given up on,

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:41.930
those who are discarded as useless... 
They all fall down here.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.550
But...

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.440
No matter where you go,

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:49.480
City is all about competition.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:53.900
That goes for this underground facility, too.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.420
Those who lose will fall even lower.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.230
For the sake of City... Dig, dig, and keep digging!

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.160
Someday, this will become the 
new home to the Commons.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:09.660
When that happens, you'll probably 
be made to dig even deeper.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.830
N-No...

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:16.730
I... I want to return to the surface!

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:20.510
This time, I'll beat Yuya Sakaki and 
become a Duel Chaser again!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.520
But I already gave you a chance.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.480
I said you could return if you beat them.

00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:30.300
One more chance... A chance 
to return to the surface!

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.280
You get only one chance!

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:36.670
If you want to return to the surface,

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.120
you must win your way up from the bottom.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.730
And let me say, those at the bottom 
deal with losers their way.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:46.100
Just getting back here will be rather difficult...

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.150
If you understand, get going!

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.380
Hold it!

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.510
Let that man go.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:02.940
My, my... So it's the legendary

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:06.740
Enjoy Chojiro and Dennis's pal.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.990
I suppose you haven't had your 
welcome ceremony yet...

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:12.920
Ready to try it now?

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.850
If you can beat everyone here in a duel,

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:18.660
you can go right back up to the surface.

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:21.580
Give me a break... Welcome party?

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:25.620
Ganging up on someone to pound 
them into the dirt is just bullying!

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:27.140
You cowards!

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:30.460
Cowards? What a nasty thing to say.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:34.120
I'm giving you all a big chance.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:38.120
In mere minutes, you can do something 
that normally takes years.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.440
You don't get a chance like this every day.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.650
This man also knew that.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.860
But then, it seemed he looked down 
on the other men here.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.640
"No matter how the Commons flock together,

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:55.860
they can't beat a former
 Tops like me," he thought.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.620
But now you understand, don't you?

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:03.340
Where you really stand.

00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:06.440
Stop prattling on and on...

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.270
Who do you think you are?

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:11.130
Last time we met, you called yourself a promoter.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.320
What are you doing here, then?

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:18.560
Good question... I suppose you 
could say I'm recycling trash.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.220
Recycling?

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:23.260
Trash? Are you talking about us?!

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:24.490
Yes.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:30.270
Duelists deemed worthless in the world 
above are stigmatized and abandoned.

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:33.870
But even within that pile of garbage,

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.550
you sometimes find a shining diamond.

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:41.010
To find them is my job.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:42.760
And what if you do?

00:06:42.760 --> 00:06:46.410
Send them into more of those 
illegal underground duels?

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:47.520
That's one possibility.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.840
But the real gems get presented to the king.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.820
The king?

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.220
The man in charge here,

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.800
Public Order Bureau Director 
Jean Michel Roget.

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:05.640
When the police cracked down on 
the underground duel venue,

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:10.640
I was able to get away because 
Roget tipped me off in advance.

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.540
That's how good the terms we're on are.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:17.550
So you give him duelists to make 
him look the other way?

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.680
You really are a coward!

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:21.250
But why?

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:24.890
Good question... Not even I know his final goal.

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:28.990
But I do know that he wants strong duelists.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:34.440
Incidentally, that man Sergey, 
the Friendship Cup participant,

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.780
is one such offering I've given him.

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:43.880
Now, let's introduce the duelists 
for our third match.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.920
Damon Lopez!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:52.480
And Sergey Volkov!

00:08:02.530 --> 00:08:04.410
Hey... She said, "Sergey"?

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:05.630
That Sergey?

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:08.680
Also known as the "Duelist Crusher."

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:13.710
Before I found him, he was an 
infamous criminal in City.

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:18.430
Pro or amateur, he challenged any
 noteworthy duelist he could find,

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:21.010
and crushed every one of them.

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.340
Of course, security came after him.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:26.520
Apparently, it took twenty of 
them to take him in.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:32.090
But then he crushed over thirty prisoners in jail.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:34.490
And so, he was sent even 
lower, to the underground.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.560
And in the welcome-party duel I held here,

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.790
he crushed an unbelievable 
fifty or more duelists.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:45.680
Fifty or more?

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.170
All by himself?

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.140
I immediately contacted Roget.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:53.440
And Roget immediately took him out,

00:08:53.440 --> 00:08:55.850
as if he knew it were going to happen.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.500
It is about to start.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:04.390
The first step toward making my plan a reality.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.010
Damon versus Sergey...

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:15.230
Which leaves only Kurosaki and Dennis.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.200
I see.

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.990
I'll be going.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:24.180
Since no Lancers are participating 
in this duel, you don't mind, right?

00:09:24.180 --> 00:09:26.330
As you wish.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.150
But may I ask where you're going?

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:30.300
Just getting some fresh air.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.360
He died?

00:09:37.850 --> 00:09:40.760
You're saying Sergey died once before?

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:44.230
It's only a rumor. However...

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:48.620
Sergey is the Duelist Crusher, who crushes 
any opponent he encounters.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:53.310
Such a dangerous man, yet Roget 
has him completely at heel.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:55.740
Almost like he's a different person...

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:58.640
You're saying he can control minds?

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:03.080
By the way, you mentioned something earlier 
about being from another dimension.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.130
Have you ever heard this?

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:10.510
There's a rumor that Roget also 
came from another dimension.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:13.060
From another dimension?

00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:15.760
Well, I don't know if it's true.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:19.460
But there are many strange 
rumors about that man.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:22.200
That he appeared in City out of the blue.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.550
That he was so fast to become head of security

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:30.590
because he brought the Administrative Council

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:34.700
all kinds of previously unseen technologies.

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:39.530
It's true that when I was arrested for fraud,

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.520
we didn't have any of this Real Solid Vision stuff.

00:10:45.550 --> 00:10:49.220
Riding duel... Acceleration!

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:51.980
Duel!

00:10:52.830 --> 00:10:56.270
You're saying Roget brought that technology 
from another dimension?

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:58.240
Then, Roget is...

00:11:05.940 --> 00:11:10.080
Alien Shocktrooper's attack 
takes out his last monster!

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.580
Now, all of Sergey's monsters are destroyed!

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:17.980
Duelist Crusher, my eye!

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:20.290
This is so boring, I'm basically yawning.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:22.760
One-sided losses are totally boring!

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:25.230
At least fight back a little!

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:27.050
No way...

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:32.100
Since being taken in by security, looks like 
Sergey has been defanged.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:34.070
Defanged, you say?

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:36.540
We shall see about that.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.120
All I care about is that nothing 
interferes with my trade...

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:44.740
If he'll be my backer to that end,

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:49.020
I'll gladly sift out the duelists 
he wants from the trash.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:53.820
If you won't face the welcoming party, 
I'll close shop for the day.

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:55.490
Is that all right with you?

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:01.500
I'm giving you a big chance to 
get back to the surface.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.000
What a pair of cowards you are—

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.800
Boss, Mr. Gallagher's right.

00:12:09.280 --> 00:12:12.540
If you want to get back to the surface 
quick, you've gotta win.

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:15.240
You ended up here, too?

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:19.520
Forgive me! I failed to meet your expectations!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.040
We'll face you...

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:26.570
If you feel any sense of obligation 
to us, please oblige us.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:30.500
Though if we win, we'll be the 
ones Director Roget hires.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.430
What was that?

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.470
You think I'd lose to you?

00:12:34.470 --> 00:12:35.950
Say that again!

00:12:35.090 --> 00:12:36.140
Stop it!

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:38.690
I want to hear you say that again!

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:37.770
Everyone calm down!

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:40.720
I heard everything.

00:12:48.560 --> 00:12:51.180
If I win, I can get back to the surface?

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:53.600
Then, I guess we gotta do it.

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.720
I'll fight anyone!

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:57.460
Sawatari!

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.770
I see we have a spirited one among us.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.930
I can't wait.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.130
This is easy.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:21.380
I'm gonna blast past the first round!

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.390
Yeah! Get him!

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:25.130
Sergey's so weak, it's boring!

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:26.350
Crush him right now!

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:28.920
No... This isn't a duel.

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:31.890
Being happy, watching someone else get hurt...

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:39.400
But... I did the same thing.

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:45.600
The rumors are likely true.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:48.750
Roget surely came from the Fusion Dimension.

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.310
He came from Academia.

00:13:53.750 --> 00:13:55.120
You've done good work,

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:57.980
but I need you to continue gathering 
information underground.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:02.520
And periodically report on the status 
of the Lancers members.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:03.500
Sir.

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:07.590
W-Wait!

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:21.880
U-Um...

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:25.420
Do not falter!

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.550
I want to apologize.

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:33.650
To you... And to my brother.

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:35.050
Apologize?

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:41.460
I was supposed to fight, 
but Tsukikage went instead...

00:14:41.830 --> 00:14:43.530
Don't worry.

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:47.430
I sent Tsukikage, with a plan in mind.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.500
But I...

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:52.400
I did something awful to Tsukikage.

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:54.070
Awful?

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:57.400
I wished for you to lose.

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.820
Because you were fighting in my place.

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:02.380
I...

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:06.850
I want to be useful to my brother, too!

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.130
Like you are.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.320
I want to become someone he trusts.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:16.030
Someday... Someday...

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:20.000
So that, someday, I can see you gallantly duel.

00:15:21.640 --> 00:15:25.320
I want you both to see me like that...

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:26.800
And Yuya, too!

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.770
Yuya Sakaki?

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:47.630
Um... What... just happened?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.430
Damon was winning until 
just a second ago, right?

00:15:57.430 --> 00:16:00.270
Sergey was completely on the defensive...

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:02.680
So why did Sergey win?

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.010
Did Damon make a mistake?

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:08.980
It means he hasn't been defanged.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:15.520
Though he seems rather dissatisfied.

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:23.930
A-Anyway, the winner is Sergey!

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:29.200
From a huge deficit, he crushed Damon 
with a miraculous turnaround!

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:35.820
Now, one more person is 
being sent underground...

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:43.370
Who's there?

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:44.460
It is I.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:47.040
Tsukikage?! How?

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:47.990
Are the others okay?

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:50.690
Do not worry. They are safe.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:54.140
I see... I'm so glad!

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.190
What about Gongenzaka and the rest?

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:58.930
Mr. Tokumatsu and Sawatari... 
Did they escape with you?

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:00.570
No.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:04.640
No? You mean you escaped alone? Why?

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:08.640
My duty is to gather information underground.

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.940
After making my report to Master Reiji Akaba,

00:17:10.940 --> 00:17:14.110
I shall return and resume my mission.

00:17:14.440 --> 00:17:15.440
Mission...

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:18.910
Then, Reiji intentionally switched you with Layra?

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.190
But gathering information?

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.820
Aren't you going to try to save our friends?

00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:25.790
I shall.

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:33.530
Had Master Reiji the same disregard for life as 
Academia, which turns people into cards,

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.630
I would have severed my ties long ago.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:37.470
He hates Academia.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:40.660
That is why he crossed dimensions to fight them.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:46.110
Such a man would never abandon those 
allies with whom he shares a purpose.

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:47.760
Tsukikage...

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:49.260
Worry not.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:53.080
I shall report all that occurs 
underground to you.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:58.440
And you must continue winning, to achieve 
victory in the Friendship Cup.

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:04.330
That is the wish of not merely Master 
Reiji, but of Layra Akaba, as well.

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:06.030
Layra?

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:10.500
Yuya protected me for a long time.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:14.230
But I made up my mind...

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:18.210
I won't run away. I'll fight, properly.

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.180
But I can't participate in the Friendship Cup.

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:24.140
So for me...

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:27.920
No, not for me...

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:33.120
Yuya should fight for himself. 
And keep winning.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:36.590
I want him to fight Jack one more time!

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:42.300
Jack won the Friendship Cup 
and surprised everyone.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.930
He did something no one had ever done.

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:50.100
He proved that even a Commons 
could make it to the top!

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:54.710
We came here to save this world.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:59.360
But no one in this dimension believes that.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.840
They don't believe in the power of the Lancers.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:03.450
To make them believe,

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.970
we have to beat Jack!

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.620
Layra said that?

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:12.730
But...

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.080
I lost to Jack once before.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:18.400
I hope I can beat him next time,

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:22.140
but I'm still not sure how to do it...

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:25.610
Jack Atlas said this.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:29.150
If you're trying to accomplish something...

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:30.510
Do not falter!

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:36.170
I see... To get him to accept the 
power of the Lancers,

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.460
I have to beat Jack!

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:44.590
I couldn't figure out why no one 
listened to me before,

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:45.430
but I finally understand.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:49.350
Tell Layra thank you.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.170
I'm going to win the Friendship Cup,

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:55.920
fight Jack once more, and win for sure!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:56.730
Impossible.

00:19:57.920 --> 00:20:01.070
Layra has already returned to the council building.

00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:04.880
I shall convey your words to him another time.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:10.350
U-Um... Then, one more thing!

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:12.820
Yuya...

00:20:24.310 --> 00:20:25.200
This is...

00:20:32.850 --> 00:20:35.110
This is a letter from Yuya?

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:38.260
"Yuzu... I finally realized.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:41.450
The reason my voice wouldn't carry, 
no matter how I screamed.

00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:46.420
And the reason Jack said my duels 
were just about self-satisfaction.

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:49.560
It's because I haven't actually 
achieved anything yet.

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:54.830
No one will pay attention to me 
unless I win, like Jack,

00:20:54.830 --> 00:20:56.760
and become a person they acknowledge.

00:20:57.650 --> 00:21:00.490
I'm not anyone in this world yet.

00:21:01.010 --> 00:21:04.600
If no one acknowledges me, then no 
matter how loud I shout...

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:09.480
If I fight a duel just for myself, 
I won't move anyone's heart.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:14.690
In order to charm the people, engage them, 
and make them smile,

00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:18.160
I need to get the viewers to acknowledge me.

00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:19.520
To achieve that...

00:21:20.440 --> 00:21:22.200
I have to beat Jack!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:27.540
And then I'll beat Academia, 
and end the dimensional war.

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:30.700
Let's go back home to everyone.

00:21:32.130 --> 00:21:33.420
I promised the principal,

00:21:33.420 --> 00:21:37.960
Futoshi, Ayu, Tatsuya, and my mom

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.710
that I'd bring you back, no matter what.

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:44.440
I'll save Gongenzaka and Sawatari, too.

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:48.360
And I won't abandon a single 
one of our other friends.

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:51.500
I'll make this a world where everyone can smile,

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:54.330
and then we'll go home...

00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:57.060
To all of our homes!"

00:21:58.100 --> 00:21:59.190
Yuya...

00:22:00.010 --> 00:22:01.360
I'll win!

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:03.000
With my style of dueling!

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:07.960
And I'll bring true smiles back to 
the hearts of City's people!

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:49.640
Kurosaki and Dennis are going to duel?

00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:52.540
We may be fellow Lancers members,

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:53.960
but let's both fight hard, okay?

00:23:54.550 --> 00:23:57.630
With this duel, we'll learn if we 
really are on the same team.

00:23:57.630 --> 00:23:59.450
So mean!

00:23:59.850 --> 00:24:03.120
I don't think he likes me very much...

00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:06.170
So I'll have to crush him thoroughly this time.

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:07.620
Thoroughly...

00:24:08.470 --> 00:24:12.390
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
The Clown's Mask.

00:24:12.800 --> 00:24:14.630
The fun is only getting started!
